.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt ECHO 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm echo
.Nd write arguments to standard output
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Op Ar string ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility writes its
.Ar string
operands to standard output, separated by single spaces, followed by a newline.
.Pp
If the first operand is exactly
.Fl n ,
it is not printed and the trailing newline is suppressed.
Other operands, including
.Dq --
and option-like strings, are printed literally.
No backslash escape processing is performed.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
utility conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008
except that backslash escape processing is not implemented in this milestone.
